// Donor: rustc `rustc_ast_lowering` -- lowering is its own module BELOW codegen, and the
//   thing that builds the IR owns it rather than the thing that prints it.
// Role: layer lower -- THE LOWERING. Tree in, IR out; it prints nothing and calls nothing
//   that prints. The architecture table allows this layer `tree`, `sem`, `types` and
//   `diag`, and no other edge.
// Used by: emit_c/ through the receiver `Lowerer` held in `Emitter.lo` -- `emit_callable`
//   drives the lowering, then walks the finished body to print it.
// Guarded by: check-novac-deps.py (the edges), check-novac-lowering-one-door.py (a value
//   shape lowered in the emitter instead of here), novac-tree-edges.py --split (the move's
//   own criterion), lower_test.nv (the graph shapes), the corpus C diff.
module novac.lower
import ../tree.{Node, NodeKind, assign_op_of}
import ../types.{TyId, is_ty}
import ../diag.{ice_at}
import ../sem.{branch_children}
import ../sem.{narrowing_of}
import ../sem.{is_expr_kind, is_println_call, is_value_tail_kind, leaf_kind, leaf_text}
import ../sem.{literal_prim_of, print_call_ends_line}
import ../sem.{iflet_pattern_at, iflet_body_at, iflet_else_at, iflet_init_at}
import ../sem.{is_option_some_pattern}
import ../sem.{loop_ctl_is_break, is_collection_head}
// The receiver's fields and the store it records (the receiver moved here from ir.nv).
import ../tree.{AssignOp}
import ../sem.{Ctx, CheckOut}


/// THE LOWERING'S RECEIVER (274.8 M3). The lowering used to live as methods on `Emitter`,
/// the printer's own state, and a method of the printer cannot live in a module BELOW the
/// printer -- that is the edge inversion the architecture table forbids. So the work is a
/// change of receiver, not a move of files, and this type is where the lowering lands.
///
/// IT CARRIES THREE THINGS: the builder under construction, plus `ctx` and `out`, which
/// the lowering asks 7 and 11 times. That is shape C of plan 274.8 section 2s, chosen by
/// measurement over two alternatives: handing `ctx`/`out` as parameters would make FIVE
/// methods accept arguments they never read purely to pass on, and taking all three fields
/// away from `Emitter` would cost 181 printer rewires against 23.
///
/// TWO READERS ARE NOT TWO SOURCES. `Emitter` keeps its own `ctx`/`out` and this type has
/// its own; that is not a second home for either, because their home is `sem` and both
/// readers are read-only. What `Emitter` LOST is the builder -- the mutable state, which
/// belongs with the methods that write it.
export type Lowerer {
    ctx Ctx /// the type registry and def table, read only -- same home as Emitter's (`sem`)
    out CheckOut /// the checker's channel: every type question is a READ here
    mut ir FnBuilder /// the body under construction -- the lowering's own mutable state
}

/// A compound or plain assignment, recorded as a statement of the body. First method to
/// live here rather than on the printer (274.8 M3, slice 1): it touches the builder and
/// nothing else, so it proves the receiver without dragging the channel along.
fn Lowerer mut @lower_store(target Node, op AssignOp, src Node) -> () {
    @ir.store(target, op, src)
}

/// A temporary of the body holding a destructuring scrutinee, with the initialiser placed
/// into it. Second method to live on the receiver (274.8 M3, slice 2), and the LAST one
/// that could move alone: the call-structure measure found only two leaves, and this is the
/// one with no outward calls at all. What remains are two mutually recursive groups plus
/// three methods that call into printing -- they move as wholes, not one at a time.
///
/// The name is the body's own index, never the author's: a destructuring scrutinee is the
/// compiler's invention, and `named` would claim otherwise (held by
/// check-novac-invented-name-not-named).
fn Lowerer mut @bind_pair_temp(init Node, pt TyId) -> Local {
    ro l = @ir.temp(pt)
    @ir.place(init, l)
    l
}

/// THE LOWERING (274.8 M3). Everything here used to be methods on `Emitter`, the printer's own
/// state, in `emit_c/`. A method of the printer cannot live in a module BELOW the printer, so
/// the move was a change of RECEIVER, not of files -- and this file is where the lowering
/// landed once the receiver existed.
///
/// WHY IT ARRIVED AS ONE PIECE. The call structure was measured first: after two leaves there
/// were no more methods that could travel alone, the core is closed under calls, and its border
/// with printing is ZERO -- nothing here calls anything that prints. Cutting a closed, mutually
/// recursive set one method at a time would leave a tree that does not build at every step.
///
/// WHAT THIS FILE MAY NOT DO. It is `lower`, so the architecture table allows it `tree`, `sem`,
/// `types` and `diag` and nothing else. A question that used to reach past that -- the name of
/// `println` -- is now asked of the channel (`sem.is_println_call`), which is where questions
/// about what a node MEANS belong anyway. Its one-time companions (`sem.is_int_lit`,
/// `sem.is_ident_leaf`) left with the D486 arc (2026-09-29): the `@pattern()` door reads the
/// tree directly, and an export nobody asks is code nobody runs (P35).

/// tail=true: the LAST expression statement of an int fn body is its return
/// value (Nova tail-expression semantics; arithmetic.nv relies on it).
fn Lowerer mut @lower_block_stmts_fn(b Node, tail bool) -> () {
    ro kids = branch_children(b)
    mut cleaned = false
    mut last_branch = -1
    if tail {
        mut j = 0
        for c in kids {
            match c {
                Leaf(_) => {}
                Branch { .. } => { last_branch = j }
            }
            j += 1
        }
    } else {
        // No tail duty: no statement of this block is a return value, and -1
        // is an index no child can equal, so the test below never fires.
    }
    mut j = 0
    for c in kids {
        match c {
            Leaf(_) => {} // the block's own braces -- trivia carriers, not statements
            Branch { .. } => {
                if tail && j == last_branch && c.kind_of() == NodeKind.MatchExpr
                        && !is_ty(@out.type_if_known(c.id_of())) {
                    // A tail match whose arms are BLOCKS yields no value --
                    // they leave through `return` (274.5 wave B9), and the
                    // checker recorded no type on purpose. The statement form
                    // is the honest emission: no result temporary, no `return`
                    // of a value nobody produced.
                    @lower_match(c, no_local())
                } else if tail && j == last_branch && @tail_places_value(c) {
                    // THE TAIL IS THE RETURNED VALUE -- one door (274.8 M1).
                    // Until M1 four arms stood here (match, if, positional
                    // record, general expression), each spelling `return`
                    // itself; the form of the value is now the printer's one
                    // dispatch (`build_value` in emit_place.nv).
                    @lower_exit_value(c, @ir.ret_place(), b.id_of())
                    cleaned = true
                } else {
                    @lower_stmt(c)
                }
            }
        }
        j += 1
    }
    // The block's end is an exit of what it bound (D432) -- unless its returned
    // value already ran them, between the value and the `return`.
    if !cleaned {
        @lower_cleanups(b.id_of(), ExitOutcome.NormalExit)
    } else {
        // `@lower_exit_value` placed them.
    }
}

/// The same door as `@lower_block_stmts_fn`'s `tail=true` path, generalized
/// to an ARBITRARY destination instead of the function's own return place --
/// written for a match arm's Block body (registry #TBD, the block-tail-arm
/// wave): the arm's tail is the value the OUTER match reads, not the
/// enclosing function's return, so `@ir.ret_place()` would be the wrong
/// local entirely.
///
/// A NEW function rather than a parameter on the existing one:
/// `@lower_block_stmts_fn` is shared with every function body's own tail,
/// and widening its signature would need its own both-ways proof on that
/// unrelated path -- this door touches nothing there, by construction.
fn Lowerer mut @lower_block_stmts_value(b Node, dest Local) -> () {
    ro kids = branch_children(b)
    mut last_branch = -1
    mut j = 0
    for c in kids {
        match c {
            Leaf(_) => {}
            Branch { .. } => { last_branch = j }
        }
        j += 1
    }
    mut i = 0
    for c in kids {
        match c {
            Leaf(_) => {} // the block's own braces -- trivia carriers, not statements
            Branch { .. } => {
                if i == last_branch && c.kind_of() == NodeKind.MatchExpr
                        && !is_ty(@out.type_if_known(c.id_of())) {
                    // A tail match whose OWN arms are Blocks yields no value
                    // (the same rule this whole door exists to grow): the
                    // checker recorded no type on purpose, so the honest
                    // emission is the statement form, exactly as
                    // `@lower_block_stmts_fn`'s twin arm does.
                    @lower_match(c, no_local())
                } else if i == last_branch && @tail_places_value(c) {
                    @lower_place(c, dest)
                } else {
                    @lower_stmt(c)
                }
            }
        }
        i += 1
    }
    // The block's end is an exit of what it bound (D432): after its value is placed.
    @lower_cleanups(b.id_of(), ExitOutcome.NormalExit)
}

/// A tail `if` laid down as a VALUE: a zero-initialised temporary, both
/// branches writing into it, the caller returning it.
///
/// The shape is `@emit_match`'s and the comment there explains the `(T){0}`:
/// a temporary that is only conditionally written answers whatever the stack
/// held otherwise -- valid C, a different number per run, no diagnostic
/// anywhere. Here BOTH branches always write, but the initialiser stays: it
/// costs one C token and removes a whole class of question.
fn Lowerer mut @lower_if_value(n Node, res_t TyId) -> Local {
    ro kids = branch_children(n)
    // The temporary is a LOCAL of the lowered body, and its DECLARATION is a statement of
    // that body (274.8 M2b-2 step 2): recorded here, printed by the one statement door. It
    // starts at zero because a branch may fall through without assigning it -- the reason
    // lives on `DeclAt.Zeroed`, with every one of its clients named there.
    ro t = @ir.temp(res_t)
    @ir.declare_zeroed(t)
    // Both branches are BLOCKS of the body with one join (274.8 M2b-1): an
    // if-value always has an else, so `has_else` is a fact, not a guess. The head goes
    // through the ONE door (M2b-2 step 3a) -- the same one the statement `if`, the
    // `if let` and a match guard use.
    ro cond = Cond.Expr(kids[1])
    // The else branch of an if-value is always a BLOCK printed as `} else {`, so it is
    // braced by construction -- not a guess, the next line prints the brace.
    ro c = @ir.begin_if(cond, ElseShape.Braced)
    @lower_block_value(kids[2], t)
    @ir.begin_else(c)
    @lower_else_value(kids[4], t)
    @ir.end_if(c)
    // The result local is HANDED BACK (274.8 M2b-2, prerequisite 5): the caller records
    // the assignment from it at LOWERING time, so nothing is lowered while the walk prints.
    t
}

/// A tail `if let` laid down as a VALUE (registry 1189): the Option into its
/// own temporary, the Some-test, the binder, and BOTH branches writing into a
/// result temporary the caller returns.
///
/// It is `@lower_if_value` and `@lower_if_let` composed, and neither of them
/// could answer alone: the first knows how a branching VALUE is laid down, the
/// second knows what an if-let's parts are. The `(T){0}` initialiser is there
/// for the reason given at `@lower_if_value` -- both branches always write, and
/// the zero costs one C token to remove the whole question.
///
/// AN `else` IS A FACT HERE, not a guess: the checker refuses a value if-let
/// without one (`IFLET_VALUE_NEEDS_ELSE_MSG`), so `kids[9]` exists by the time
/// this runs. The same holds for the recorded type -- the branches had to
/// agree before anything reached the lowering.
fn Lowerer mut @lower_if_let_value(n Node, res_t TyId) -> Local {
    ro kids = branch_children(n)
    ro init = kids[iflet_init_at(kids)]
    ro ot = @out.type_of(init.id_of())
    ro t = @ir.temp(res_t)
    @ir.declare_zeroed(t)
    // The Option is a temporary of the BODY, named by its index (274.8 M3):
    // the Option of an `if let` is the compiler's, not the author's.
    ro lo = @ir.temp(ot)
    @lower_place(init, lo)
    ro c = @ir.begin_if(@variant_test(kids[iflet_pattern_at(kids)], ot, lo), ElseShape.Braced)
    // The pattern binds through the match arm's own door (wave P3): a binder
    // reads the payload, a nested pattern reads its piece -- one judgment,
    // recorded by the checker, spelled here.
    @lower_pattern_bind(kids[iflet_pattern_at(kids)], ot, lo)
    @lower_block_value(kids[iflet_body_at(kids)], t)
    @ir.begin_else(c)
    @lower_else_value(kids[iflet_else_at(kids)], t)
    @ir.end_if(c)
    t
}

/// Emit a block whose LAST statement is its value: everything before it runs
/// as a statement, and the last one is assigned to the `if` temporary.
///
/// THE DOOR THIS WAVE HAD TO ADD, and the reason is a real difference rather
/// than an oversight in the match code: a match ARM is an expression, so
/// `@emit_arm_value` writes `t = <expr>;` in one line. An `if` BRANCH is a
/// block, and its value is whatever its last statement produces -- so the
/// block has to be walked, and only its tail turned into an assignment.
fn Lowerer mut @lower_block_value(b Node, t Local) -> () {
    ro kids = branch_children(b)
    mut last_branch = -1
    mut j = 0
    for c in kids {
        match c {
            Leaf(_) => {}
            Branch { .. } => { last_branch = j }
        }
        j += 1
    }
    j = 0
    for c in kids {
        match c {
            Leaf(_) => {} // the block's braces are trivia, not statements
            Branch { .. } => {
                if j == last_branch && @tail_places_value(c) {
                    @lower_place(c, t)
                } else {
                    // Before the tail: effect only. The tail asks the ONE door, not `is_expr_kind`
                    // -- a tuple or nested `if` tail went to `@lower_stmt` and the value was
                    // DROPPED, silently (part 5 of p274-carina-k1: `0 0` for the oracle's `6 2`).
                    @lower_stmt(c)
                }
            }
        }
        j += 1
    }
}

/// Emit one statement by node kind (call/if/while/return/bind/assign/for/expr).
fn Lowerer mut @lower_stmt(st Node) -> () {
    ro k = st.kind_of()
    // A call holding D476 temporaries (an affine value handed to a view): its
    // arguments laid down, the call run, the temporaries cleaned (ir_cleanup.nv).
    if (k == NodeKind.Call || k == NodeKind.MethodCall) && @out.cleanup_first(st.id_of()) >= 0 {
        ro cs = @d476_args(st)
        @lower_eval(st)
        @d476_cleanups(cs)
        return
    } else {
        // An ordinary statement: by kind below.
    }
    if k == NodeKind.Unsafe {
        @lower_unsafe_stmt(st)
    } else if k == NodeKind.MatchExpr {
        // A match in STATEMENT position (274.5 wave B5): the arms run for
        // effect. No result temporary is declared -- nobody asked this match
        // for a value, and emitting a variable to hold an answer no one wants
        // is the shape this compiler keeps refusing elsewhere.
        @lower_match(st, no_local())
    } else if k == NodeKind.Call {
        // A call in statement position is an EVALUATION of the lowered body
        // (274.8 M2a); its printer keeps the arguments and their hoists.
        @lower_eval(st)
    } else if k == NodeKind.IfStmt {
        // A branch of the lowered body (274.8 M2b-1): opened, filled and
        // joined through the builder's events, printed at the same events
        // (emit_flow.nv). `None`: this `if` is a statement of its block, not
        // the else branch of another.
        @lower_if(st, None)
    } else if k == NodeKind.WhileStmt {
        @lower_while(st)
    } else if k == NodeKind.WhileLet {
        @lower_while_let(st)
    } else if k == NodeKind.WithStmt {
        // E.9 step 2: install, run the body, restore on every exit (lower_with.nv).
        @lower_with(st)
    } else if k == NodeKind.SupervisedStmt {
        // E.9 step 4: a fiber scope around the body, joined on every exit.
        @lower_supervised(st)
    } else if k == NodeKind.SpawnStmt {
        // E.9 step 4: the body is a function of its own (emit_c/emit_spawn.nv).
        @ir.spawn_site(st.id_of())
    } else if k == NodeKind.RetStmt {
        @lower_return(st)
    } else if k == NodeKind.LoopCtl {
        // `break` / `continue` (274.7 B10): the block ends with the jump, what the
        // source wrote after it lands in a fresh block -- `@lower_return`'s shape.
        // The values the pass bound and still owns are cleaned first (D432 s6).
        @lower_cleanups(st.id_of(), ExitOutcome.NormalExit)
        if loop_ctl_is_break(st) {
            @ir.break_loop()
        } else {
            @ir.continue_loop()
        }
    } else if k == NodeKind.BindStmt {
        @lower_bind(st)
    } else if k == NodeKind.AssignStmt {
        // A store into a place the tree names (274.8 M2a): the target, the
        // operator and the value are recorded, the one printer spells them --
        // a compound store from the one form table, the target as an
        // expression (a name and `@field` on one path).
        ro kids = branch_children(st)
        ro src = kids[2]
        // AN `if` AS THE SOURCE LOWERS BEFORE THE STORE IS RECORDED (the
        // if-value wave): it lays down blocks of the body, and a printer
        // asked to lower would push into a FINISHED builder -- the exact
        // precedent of `@hoist_sealed_args`, whose hoist the store's printer
        // reads back through `@lo.ir.local_of_node`, so the recorded store
        // below needs no new shape.
        // A block form on the right, or nested in it, or in the target's index
        // (registry 1619): laid down first and read back by the printer.
        // The source's own arguments, in order and once, as in `@lower_place`
        // (registries 1681, 1683: `q = Pv { b: match k {..}, .. }` iced).
        @hoist_ordered_args(src)
        @hoist_sealed_args(src)
        @hoist_operand(src)
        @hoist_block_forms(kids[0])
        if src.kind_of() == NodeKind.IfExpr || src.kind_of() == NodeKind.MatchExpr {
            ro sty = @out.type_if_known(src.id_of())
            if is_ty(sty) {
                match @lower_value_source(src, sty) {
                    Some(l) => @ir.remember_hoist(src.id_of(), l)
                    None => {}
                }
            } else {
                // SILENT-OK: refused where it was typed; nothing to hoist.
            }
        } else {
            // An ordinary source prints inline, as before.
        }
        @lower_store(kids[0], assign_op_of(leaf_kind(kids[1])), src)
    } else if k == NodeKind.ForStmt {
        ro kids = branch_children(st)
        if @out.has_callee(st.id_of()) {
            // An ITERATOR head (D58): the checker recorded its `next` on the loop.
            @lower_for_iter(st, kids)
            return
        }
        if is_collection_head(kids[3]) {
            // A COLLECTION head (wave B16) walks a vector by index: a loop
            // of the lowered body whose header carries the collection, the
            // index and the element locals (274.8 M2b-1c, emit_flow.nv). A
            // name or field head costs one pointer copy into the temporary --
            // the same one-evaluation contract a call head needs for its
            // effects.
            @lower_for_each(kids)
            return
        }
        // A RANGE head: a loop of the lowered body with the range as its
        // header form (274.8 M2b-1, emit_flow.nv).
        @lower_for_range(kids)
    } else if is_value_tail_kind(k) {
        // An expression in statement position -- a positional record
        // included -- is an EVALUATION of the lowered body (274.8 M2a): built
        // where it needs building, dropped, the effects in written order.
        @lower_eval(st)
    } else if k == NodeKind.DestructureBind {
        @lower_destructure_bind(st)
    } else if k == NodeKind.IfLet {
        // An if-let is a branch of the lowered body testing `IsSome` of the
        // local its Option landed in (274.8 M2b-1b, emit_flow.nv).
        @lower_if_let(st, None)
    } else {
        ice_at("novac/src/lower/lowering.nv:423", "emit: statement kind outside the subset")
    }
}

/// Binding. A record-constructor initializer follows the oracle's tmp scheme
/// (fixed point on records.nv); a match initializer follows the match
/// scheme; everything else is a plain typed local.
fn Lowerer mut @lower_bind(st Node) -> () {
    ro kids = branch_children(st)
    ro vname = leaf_text(kids[1])
    ro init = kids[kids.len() - 1]
    ro vtype = @out.type_of(init.id_of())
    // ONE DOOR (274.8 M1): the binding is a local of the lowered body, and its
    // initializer lands in it through `place`. Until M1 six arms stood here --
    // match, if-expression, array literal, positional record, constructor,
    // general expression -- each spelling the declaration line itself.
    ro l = @ir.named(vtype, vname)
    @lower_place(init, l)
    // An exit below may clean this value (D432): the statement names its local -- and,
    // cleaned on some paths only, its drop flag (s5): zero here, set by each move.
    if @out.cleanups.len() > 0 {
        mut gone = no_local()
        if @out.has_cond(st.id_of()) {
            gone = @ir.temp(@ctx.prims.int_id)
            @ir.declare_zeroed(gone)
        } else {
            // Cleaned unconditionally wherever it is cleaned: no flag.
        }
        @ir.remember_binding(st.id_of(), l, gone)
    } else {
        // Nothing is cleaned in this file: no exit asks.
    }
}

/// A destructuring binding: the scrutinee lands in a temporary ONCE, and the
/// pattern binds out of it through the ONE recursive door (D486,
/// lower_match.nv) -- the same walk the match arm takes, minus the tests:
/// the checker held this position to irrefutable forms (D486 §4), so there
/// is nothing to test, only bindings to lay down.
///
/// ONCE is the whole contract, and it is the same one V3-1 proved for the
/// constructor: `ro (a, b) = mk()` calls `mk` a single time, so a side effect
/// in it prints once. A shape that re-read the scrutinee per name would be
/// correct on pure values and silently wrong on effectful ones.
fn Lowerer mut @lower_destructure_bind(st Node) -> () {
    ro kids = branch_children(st)
    ro pat = kids[1]
    ro init = kids[kids.len() - 1]
    ro pt = @out.type_of(init.id_of())
    // ALWAYS THROUGH A LOCAL (M3c). The construction case no longer needs its own line
    // here: `@ir.place` records the initializer, and the assignment printer builds a
    // construction in its own `Expr` arm. One door instead of two, and the base of every
    // projection below is a LOCAL -- which is what lets the reads become statements.
    ro base = @lower_value_source(init, pt) ?? @bind_pair_temp(init, pt)
    @lower_pattern_bind(pat, pt, base)
}

/// One `if` statement with its `else` / `else if` chain. `outer` is the
/// enclosing `if` when this one IS its else branch: then the else branch is
/// opened first and the chained `if` shares the outer join.
fn Lowerer mut @lower_if(st Node, outer Option[IfCtx]) -> () {
    ro kids = branch_children(st)
    ro has_else = kids.len() > 4
    // The condition is RECORDED first and PRINTED from the record (M2b-2 step 3a): the
    // printing no longer reads the tree, which is what lets one walk print every branch
    // later. Recording before printing is safe because printing a condition lowers
    // nothing -- `emit_expr` touches neither the builder nor the name counter (measured
    // 2026-09-08); only `build_value` lowers, and a condition never goes through it.
    // A block form in the condition is laid down before the test (registry 1619);
    // a chained `else if` with one is lowered braced instead (`else_shape`).
    @hoist_operand(kids[1])
    ro cond = Cond.Expr(kids[1])
    ro shape = else_shape(kids, 4)
    ro c = match outer {
        None => @ir.begin_if(cond, shape)
        // THE door for "else, then a chain" -- until 2026-09-08 this pair was opened by
        // hand here and in `lower_if_let`, while the door itself had only a test as its
        // caller (class #991: one concept, two implementations).
        Some(o) => @ir.begin_else_if(o, cond, shape)
    }
    // ONE shape of else (M2b-2-0): a chained `if` continues the `} else ` line its
    // caller printed, so it starts without the indent the top-level `if` carries.
    // A NARROWING `if x is T` (D54): the branch opens with `x` unboxed into a
    // binding of the same name -- through a temporary, since C reads a
    // declarator's own name inside its initializer.
    match narrowing_of(kids[1], @out, @ctx) {
        Some(nw) => {
            ro tmp = @ir.temp(nw.target)
            @ir.unbox_any(tmp, nw.subject)
            @ir.copy(@ir.named(nw.target, nw.name), tmp)
        }
        None => {} // no narrowing: the branch reads the names as they are
    }
    @lower_block_stmts_fn(kids[2], false)
    if has_else {
        // The closing brace and the `else` share one line -- the one shape of else
        // (M2b-2-0). Until then the statement `if` printed `}` and `else` on two lines
        // while the if-value printed `} else {`; the oracle's recorded C has 41 753
        // `} else {` and no bare `else {`, so the second shape was novac's own, and a
        // single printing walk would have needed a flag to reproduce it.
        // The ELSE branch, since 2026-08-18. Before that the parser did not
        // read `else` at all; reading it without writing it here would have
        // been worse than not reading it -- the branch would vanish from the
        // C in silence, which is the class this compiler keeps finding in
        // others.
        @lower_else_tail(c, kids[4])
    } else {
        // No else branch was written: the else block IS the join.
    }
    @ir.end_if(c)
}

/// What follows `else` -- ONE door for the `if` and the `if let` (until
/// M2b-1b each printed its own copy of this and the two had drifted: the `if`
/// iced on an `else if let` tail the `if let` accepted). Three shapes are
/// legal and ALL are named: a block, a chained `if`, a chained `if let`.
/// Anything else is an invariant break, and it says so -- an `else` standing
/// for "every other node kind" is what P21 refuses, because the next kind
/// added to the tree would quietly land in it.
fn Lowerer mut @lower_else_tail(c IfCtx, tail Node) -> () {
    // The caller printed `    } else ` already: this door prints only what follows.
    ro tk = tail.kind_of()
    if tk == NodeKind.Block {
        @ir.begin_else(c)
        @lower_block_stmts_fn(tail, false)
    } else if tk == NodeKind.IfStmt && contains_block_form(branch_children(tail)[1]) {
        // The braced shape `else_shape` chose: the `if` stands alone in the else block.
        @ir.begin_else(c)
        @lower_if(tail, None)
    } else if tk == NodeKind.IfStmt {
        @lower_if(tail, Some(c))
    } else if tk == NodeKind.IfLet {
        // C has no `else <declaration>`: the chained if-let's FIRST line is
        // the declaration of its Option temporary, and printed bare after
        // `else` it is not a statement -- clang refuses the unit. Found by
        // the M2b-1b probe (2026-09-06): the two copies of this tail had
        // accepted the form and printed it unbraced since the else branch
        // was added, and no corpus file carried it (registry #991: one
        // concept, two implementations, the copy not knowing a fact the
        // original knew). The braces give the temporary a block of its own;
        // the IR already had that block -- the outer else.
        @lower_if_let(tail, Some(c))
    } else {
        ice_at("novac/src/lower/lowering.nv:566", "emit: the else branch is neither a block nor a chained if / if-let")
    }
}

/// One `if Some(v) = expr { ... }` (wave M2b-1b, from emit_iflet.nv): the
/// Option lands in its own binding through the placement door, the branch
/// tests `IsSome` of that local, and the binder is a binding local assigned
/// the payload -- three IR statements where the printer used to spell three
/// lines by hand. The C is the same: `T tmp = <init>;`, the Some-test
/// through the ONE Option door (emit_option.nv, wave W4), `P v = tmp.value;`.
/// INTEROP, named as such: `.tag`/`.value` are the shell's Option ABI
/// (`NovaOpt_X{.tag,.value}`, read off shell.tpl.c); goes the day novac emits
/// the whole prelude.
fn Lowerer mut @lower_if_let(st Node, outer Option[IfCtx]) -> () {
    ro kids = branch_children(st)
    ro init = kids[iflet_init_at(kids)]
    ro ot = @out.type_of(init.id_of())
    ro else_at = iflet_else_at(kids)
    ro has_else = kids.len() > else_at
    // THE ELSE BRANCH IS OPENED BY THE DOOR, NOT HERE (fix 2026-09-08, ICE «a block sealed
    // twice (it already jumps)» on `novac/fixtures/iflet_else/pos_2.nv`). Until the door
    // `@begin_else_if` existed, this function opened the pair «else, then a chain» by hand:
    // `begin_else` here, the chained `if` below. The door now does BOTH, so the call here was
    // the second half of a pair whose first half had moved -- `begin_else` ran twice and the
    // second `@close` hit a block already sealed with `Goto`. The door stays whole; the
    // leftover half goes. For a non-chained if-let (`outer == None`) nothing changes at all.
    //
    // A temporary of the body, named by its index (274.8 M3): the Option of an
    // `if let` is the compiler's, not the author's.
    ro lo = @ir.temp(ot)
    // Recorded first, printed from the record -- the same door the plain `if` uses
    // (M2b-2 step 3a). The head is identical to what this function spelled by hand:
    // `option_some_test` reads the local's type and name, which is what it was passed.
    ro cond = @variant_test(kids[iflet_pattern_at(kids)], ot, lo)
    ro shape = else_shape(kids, else_at)
    // THE TEMPORARY BELONGS TO THE ELSE BLOCK, and under the walk that is decided by
    // MEMBERSHIP rather than by the moment of printing (found 2026-09-09, the last divergence
    // of step 3b: `NovaOpt T2 = b;` printed one line ABOVE its `} else {` in
    // `novac/fixtures/iflet_else/pos_2.nv`). The note this replaced said the declaration
    // `belongs to the block that precedes the branch` -- true while printing was immediate,
    // false once the walk prints from sealed blocks: for a CHAIN that preceding block is the
    // outer then-branch.
    //
    // So the composition `begin_else_if` is UNROLLED across these three steps, and the
    // statement lands between its halves. This is not a return to the shape that iced on
    // 2026-09-08 (`a block sealed twice (it already jumps)`): that defect was `begin_else`
    // running TWICE -- by hand here and again inside the door. Each half runs exactly once.
    match outer {
        None => {
            // Not chained: nothing to open, the temporary belongs where the source wrote it.
        }
        Some(o) => @ir.begin_else(o)
    }
    @lower_place(init, lo)
    ro c = match outer {
        None => @ir.begin_if(cond, shape)
        Some(o) => @ir.begin_chained_if(cond, o.join, shape)
    }
    // NOT chained for the purpose of PRINTING, even when `outer` is Some -- braced, not continued.
    // A chained plain `if` continues the `} else ` line its caller printed, so it carries no
    // indent; a chained `if let` is wrapped in braces by `lower_else_tail` (`{` before it,
    // `    }` after), because C has no `else <declaration>` and an if-let's first line IS the
    // declaration of its Option temporary -- unbraced, clang refuses the unit (registry
    // #991, found by the M2b-1b probe). Inside those braces the head starts a NEW line and
    // keeps its indent. Measured, not reasoned: passing `chained_of(outer)` here made the
    // corpus C differ in exactly one file (fixtures/iflet_else/pos_2), the hunk being this
    // lost indent.
    // The pattern binds through the match arm's own door (wave P3) -- the
    // value door above says why.
    @lower_pattern_bind(kids[iflet_pattern_at(kids)], ot, lo)
    @lower_block_stmts_fn(kids[iflet_body_at(kids)], false)
    if has_else {
        @lower_else_tail(c, kids[else_at])
    } else {
        // No else branch was written: the else block IS the join.
    }
    @ir.end_if(c)
}

/// The HEAD TEST of a variant pattern in `if let` / `while let`: `Some` over an
/// Option keeps the Option door's spelling (`Cond.IsSome`); any other variant,
/// of any sum, is the match arm's head test (`Cond.Holds`, emit_match.nv) --
/// one test per pattern, whichever statement asks.
fn Lowerer @variant_test(pat Node, ty TyId, lo Local) -> Cond {
    if is_option_some_pattern(@ctx, pat, ty) {
        return Cond.IsSome(lo)
    }
    Cond.Holds(PatTest { pat: @pattern_of(pat, ty), scr: lo })
}

/// One `return`: the value lands in the return place through the one door
/// (274.8 M1) -- a bare `return` spells the unit itself -- and the block ends
/// with `Return`; what the source wrote after it lands in a fresh block.
fn Lowerer mut @lower_return(st Node) -> () {
    ro kids = branch_children(st)
    if kids.len() > 1 {
        @lower_exit_value(kids[1], @ir.ret_place(), st.id_of())
    } else {
        // A BARE `return` RECORDS AND PRINTS NOTHING HERE (2026-09-09). It used to print
        // `return NOVA_UNIT;` on the spot, and under the walk that landed the line right
        // after the opening brace -- before every statement -- so the function returned
        // immediately and skipped its body. Legal Nova, wrong C, and no corpus file had
        // the form: a grep for a bare `return` found zero carriers, which is why every
        // green measurement of this wave was silent about it. The `Return` terminator is
        // what the walk prints from, and it prints the same for a body that just ends.
    }
    if kids.len() <= 1 {
        // A bare `return`: the values still owned are cleaned before it (D432).
        @lower_cleanups(st.id_of(), ExitOutcome.NormalExit)
    } else {
        // `@lower_exit_value` cleaned them between the value and the return.
    }
    @ir.ret()
}


/// Records `dest = e` in the lowered body and prints it at once -- the
/// streaming bridge of waves M1/M2a: statements are lowered and printed one
/// by one until M2b prints sealed blocks.
fn Lowerer mut @lower_place(e Node, dest Local) -> () {
    // A call holding D476 temporaries (ir_cleanup.nv): its arguments laid down first,
    // its value placed in a temporary, then they go, and only then does the value reach
    // `dest` -- which may be the return place, whose assignment the printer spells as
    // the `return` itself. HERE and not at the binding: every value door -- a binding,
    // a body's or a branch's tail -- comes through this one, and a door that skipped it
    // would drop the cleanups silently (the tail did, on the first probe).
    ro cs = @d476_args(e)
    if cs.len() == 0 {
        @lower_place_value(e, dest)
        return
    } else {
        // D476 temporaries: the value waits in a temporary.
    }
    ro t = @ir.temp(@ir.decl_of(dest).ty)
    @lower_place_value(e, t)
    @d476_cleanups(cs)
    @ir.copy(dest, t)
}

/// `dest = e` once the D476 temporaries, if any, are laid down (`@lower_place`).
fn Lowerer mut @lower_place_value(e Node, dest Local) -> () {
    // A CALL IN VALUE POSITION NEEDS ITS ARGUMENTS ORDERED TOO (F65). The first
    // edition put the hoist only in `@lower_eval`, the STATEMENT door, and the
    // probe said so at once: `ro s = take(left(), right())` still printed right
    // before left, because a binding initializer comes through here instead.
    // One form, two doors -- and only the probe could tell me the second one.
    @hoist_ordered_args(e)
    @hoist_sealed_args(e)
    // A block form NESTED in the value goes first, in order (registry 1619).
    @hoist_block_forms(e)
    // THE SOURCE IS RESOLVED FIRST (prerequisite 5): a value form that lays down blocks
    // is lowered NOW and the assignment reads the local it produced, through the operand
    // rvalue door `@ir.copy`. Otherwise the tree node stays the source -- the M1 bridge,
    // printed inline by `@emit_expr`.
    match @lower_value_source(e, @ir.decl_of(dest).ty) {
        Some(l) => @ir.copy(dest, l)
        None => @ir.place(e, dest)
    }
}

/// Records an expression evaluated for its effects.
///
/// `println` IS NOT AN ORDINARY CALL and does not go through `eval` (M3a): its output
/// interleaves with the effects of building its arguments, and that interleaving is
/// observable, so it becomes a SEQUENCE of statements rather than one expression the
/// printer takes apart.
fn Lowerer mut @lower_eval(e Node) -> () {
    if is_println_call(e) {
        @lower_println(e)
        return
    }
    @hoist_ordered_args(e)
    @hoist_sealed_args(e)
    // A statement that IS a block form (`o ?? f()`, `x?`) is laid down, its value
    // dropped; one that holds one has it laid down first (registry 1619).
    @hoist_operand(e)
    if needs_own_lowering(e) { return }
    @ir.eval(e)
}

/// Lowers one `println` into the sequence it IS: per argument, whatever the argument needs
/// laid down first, then that argument's own output statement; one newline at the end.
///
/// WHY A SEQUENCE AND NOT ONE CALL. Hoisting the whole call up front ran a constructor
/// argument's effects AHEAD of its neighbours' prints -- the oracle printed `head` then
/// ticked, novac ticked first (hunt emit_c x K1, finding H1). The order of output against
/// argument effects is therefore observable, and an observable order belongs in the
/// channel: here each argument's lowering lands immediately before ITS OWN output
/// statement, so the interleaving holds by construction instead of by the printer's care.
///
/// A construction (an array literal, a record or positional record, an interpolation) is
/// still printed from the tree and hoisted by the printer right before its own output line
/// -- that is legal, because a hoist only PRINTS TEXT and print order is the walk's order.
/// `??` is the one form that could not stay: it LOWERS. It leaves through the one door
/// above, and this is why the two refusals of step 3b close.
fn Lowerer mut @lower_println(call Node) -> () {
    for c in branch_children(call) {
        ro ck = c.kind_of()
        if ck == NodeKind.Lit {
            // THE CHANNEL FIRST, AND THE FORM ONLY WHERE IT IS SILENT -- and it is silent
            // about exactly ONE literal. Measured 2026-09-09 in `check/typing.nv:836-850`:
            // the argument loop of `println` RECORDS a numeric or char literal through the
            // full `type_of` (all four kinds, plus the half where the POSITION dictates a
            // width), and skips only a STRING one -- deliberately, and its comment says why:
            // "the emitter never asks its type", because the only consumer took the pool
            // slot by shape.
            //
            // So asking the door for EVERY literal, as the first edition of this line did,
            // computed a second answer to a question the channel had already decided -- the
            // very `decide it twice` this channel's doctrine exists to prevent. Asking the
            // channel first also makes this FALLBACK DIE ON ITS OWN, and its removal
            // condition is named: when the type of a
            // string literal is published (marker `[M-strlit-node-has-no-type]`), this
            // `else` stops executing and no consumer needs editing.
            //
            // The fallback judges the LAST leaf, as the checker does: a negated literal
            // arrives as `[Minus, lit]`.
            ro known = @out.type_if_known(c.id_of())
            ro lty = if is_ty(known) {
                known
            } else {
                ro lk_kids = branch_children(c)
                literal_prim_of(leaf_kind(lk_kids[lk_kids.len() - 1]), @ctx)
            }
            @ir.output(Operand.Tree(c), lty)
        } else if is_expr_kind(ck) {
            ro ty = @out.type_of(c.id_of())
            match @lower_value_source(c, ty) {
                Some(l) => @ir.output(Operand.Place(l), ty)
                None => {
                    // A block form nested in the argument goes first (registry 1619),
                    // and so does a call's own `if`/`unsafe` argument, as in `@lower_place`
                    // (sweep 6: `println(f(if c { a } else { b }))` iced in emit).
                    // ITS OWN ARGUMENTS IN ORDER (registry 1681, D484 s2): `println`
                    // is a sequence, but each argument is still one expression.
                    @hoist_ordered_args(c)
                    @hoist_sealed_args(c)
                    @hoist_block_forms(c)
                    @ir.output(Operand.Tree(c), ty)
                }
            }
        } else {
            match c {
                Leaf(_) => {
                    // The callee leaf and the parenthesis leaves are not arguments.
                }
                Branch { .. } => {
                    // The checker refuses every branch it cannot type in an argument
                    // position (#870), so a branch here is a broken invariant rather than
                    // a shape to skip -- the silent fallout this arm replaces printed `ab`
                    // for `a20b`.
                    ice_at("novac/src/lower/lowering.nv:817", "emit_c: an argument form the checker let through (#870)")
                }
            }
        }
    }
    @ir.output_end(print_call_ends_line(call))
}

/// THE LOWERING HALF of the dispatch on the form of a value: a `match` and an `if` in value
/// position lay down blocks of the body, so they are resolved WHILE LOWERING and hand back
/// the local that holds the result. Prerequisite 5 of M2b-2 step 3b: after the walk prints
/// from sealed blocks, a printer that lowered would push into a FINISHED builder -- the
/// blocks would be recorded and never printed. The forms that only PRINT stay in
/// `build_value` below, which is the other half.
fn Lowerer mut @lower_value_source(e Node, ty TyId) -> Option[Local] {
    ro k = e.kind_of()
    if k == NodeKind.MatchExpr {
        // The match is a Switch of the lowered body (274.8 M2b-1d); its result local is
        // recorded here, assigned in each arm through the one door.
        ro t = @ir.temp(ty)
        @lower_match(e, t)
        return Some(t)
    }
    if k == NodeKind.Coalesce {
        // `??` LOWERS -- it lays down a Some-test with two branches -- so it cannot be
        // printed inline, and under the walk of step 3b a printer that lowered would push
        // into a FINISHED builder. That is not a guess: the door refused with
        // `lower: a block sealed twice (it already returns)` on both corpus carriers of the
        // form `println(x ?? y)` (measured 2026-09-09). Answering here puts `??` on the ONE
        // door for every value position at once -- the class, not the two carriers.
        return Some(@lower_coalesce(e))
    }
    // `x?` (D85) lays down the same Some-test, and its None branch RETURNS (lower_coalesce.nv).
    if k == NodeKind.Try { return Some(@lower_try(e)) }
    // `a && b` / `a || b` whose right side holds one: a branch (lower_hoist.nv, 1619).
    if needs_own_lowering(e) { return Some(@lower_short_circuit(e)) }
    if k == NodeKind.IfExpr || k == NodeKind.IfStmt {
        // A tail `if` and an if-expression lay down the same pair (wave B14); the door
        // hands back the local it declared.
        return Some(@lower_if_value(e, ty))
    }
    if k == NodeKind.IfLet {
        // The same pair with the Option machinery around it (registry 1189).
        return Some(@lower_if_let_value(e, ty))
    }
    if k == NodeKind.Unsafe { return Some(@lower_unsafe_value(e, ty)) }
    None
}

/// Whether a block's last statement is its VALUE: an expression, a positional
/// record, a tail `if`, or a match the checker typed (an untyped tail match is
/// a statement whose arms leave through `return`, 274.5 wave B9).
fn Lowerer @tail_places_value(c Node) -> bool {
    ro k = c.kind_of()
    // An `if let` places a value only when the checker TYPED it as one --
    // the same test the tail match takes, and for the same reason: the
    // statement spelling of both shapes leaves through `return`, and asking
    // the node's kind alone cannot tell the two apart.
    is_value_tail_kind(k) || k == NodeKind.IfStmt ||
        ((k == NodeKind.MatchExpr || k == NodeKind.IfLet) &&
            is_ty(@out.type_if_known(c.id_of())))
}

/// WHICH SHAPE OF `else` THIS `if` HAS -- the ONE place that decides it. A question about
/// the SHAPE of a node, so it travels with the lowering. It lived in `emit_c/` as a private
/// helper and was almost left behind: the closure measure counted `@method(` calls and a free
/// function is invisible to it.
///
/// IT TAKES THE CHILDREN AND AN INDEX, not the tail node, and that is not a detail of taste.
/// Until 2026-09-13 both callers wrote the same line by hand --
/// `if has_else { else_is_braced(kids[N]) } else { false }` -- two verbatim copies of one
/// rule, in `lower_if` and in `lower_if_let`, which would not have followed a change to
/// either. The first version of this door took `(has_else, tail)` and BROKE: arguments are
/// evaluated before the call, so `kids[4]` on an `if` without an else indexed past the end
/// and four tests said so ("index 4 out of bounds for length 3"). The old hand-written line
/// was lazy BY SHAPE -- the indexing sat inside the branch -- and a guard moved into the
/// function cannot protect an argument computed outside it.
///
/// With the index, both questions are answered by ONE reading of the length, and they were
/// one question all along: every caller's `has_else` was literally `kids.len() > N` for the
/// same N it then indexed with.
fn else_shape(kids []Node, tail_at int) -> ElseShape {
    if kids.len() <= tail_at {
        return ElseShape.NoElse
    }
    // Bound first: the index expression is not a receiver the method table accepts
    // (`E_RECV_METHOD_MISMATCH` on `Vec`), and binding it also names the thing.
    ro tail = kids[tail_at]
    ro k = tail.kind_of()
    // An `else if` whose condition holds a block form cannot chain: its condition's
    // blocks need a place to stand, and `} else if (` has none (registry 1619).
    ro braced_if = k == NodeKind.IfStmt && contains_block_form(branch_children(tail)[1])
    if k == NodeKind.Block || k == NodeKind.IfLet || braced_if {
        ElseShape.Braced
    } else {
        ElseShape.Chained
    }
}
